<section begin="intro"/>[[Buffing Fields]] (internally named <code>Shield</code>) are zones/entities which will modify the properties of any weapon damage coming through, that includes:<br/>
*[[Projectile]], [[Hitscan]], and [[Continuous Weapon|Beam]] shots from [[Weapons]] and [[Heavy Weapon]]s.
*''Some'' [[Area of Effect]] shots, only if its [[Projectile]] form gets the buff first.
**Standalone explosions that are already underway and happen to hit a buffing field do '''not''' benefit from it.
**Initial hit and explosion apply status separately.
*''Some'' projectile-based [[Abilities]], [[Augments]], and [[Precept]]s.
*''Some'' projectile-based melee attacks.
**[[Glaive (Weapon Type)]], {{Weapon|Deconstructor}}, and {{Weapon|Wolf Sledge}} throws do '''not''' benefit.
*''Some'' operator [[Amps]].
**[[Phahd Scaffold]] does '''not''' benefit.
**Elemental damage bonuses do '''not''' improve [[Eidolon]] shield damage (unless it's a {{D|Void}} damage bonus).
*Projectile-using [[Specter]]s, [[Companions]], Summons, and allied NPCs.
**They should be standing inside or close to a buffing field to benefit effectively.
*''Some'' projectile-based [[Gear]].
[[AoE]] attacks may benefit partially or not at all, even if the projectile does.<br/>
Usually a buffing field will grant 2 or more enhancements, and will prevent the projectile from receiving benefits of buffing fields from other sources.<section end="intro"/>
