==Targets==
This table will only list unexpected/ambiguous things that can or can't benefit from a buffing field, such as [[Abilities]] and [[:Category:Melee Weapons|Melee Weapons]].<br/>
If a melee is not in this table - it ''probably'' does '''not''' benefit; if a primary is not in this table - it ''probably'' '''does''' benefit; and so on.<br/>
The table is still incomplete, and as the banner says - '''this page is actively being worked on'''. See also [[#Required Research]].<br/>
The best way to buff [[:Category:Spawning Projectiles|Spawning Projectiles]] and [[:Category:Splitting Projectiles|Splitting Projectiles]] is to create a buffing field on their origin (which is often an enemy), otherwise they do '''not''' benefit.<br/>
Almost all main-fire [[AoE]] explosions from various weapons and abilities seem to maybe benefit but '''not''' apply forced [[procs]].
